' Figure 4.5: Sequence Diagram – Collaboration Request Workflow
@startuml
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ParticipantBorderColor #161311
    ActorBackgroundColor #FAF8F5
    ActorBorderColor #161311
    LifeLineBorderColor #161311
    ArrowColor #161311
}

actor "Applicant Student" as Applicant
participant "React Frontend\n(Workspace/Discovery)" as React
participant "Express REST API\n(requestController)" as API
database "MongoDB Database\n(Collections)" as DB
actor "Project Owner" as Owner

Applicant -> React : Click "Apply to Join" (message)
React -> API : POST /api/projects/:id/requests { message }
activate API

API -> DB : Find Project & existing Requests
activate DB
DB --> API : Project details & Request list
deactivate DB

API -> API : Validate OPEN status, not owner, not member, no pending duplicate
API -> DB : Create CollaborationRequest (status: PENDING)
activate DB
DB --> API : Request saved
deactivate DB

API --> React : 201 Created { success: true, data: request }
deactivate API
React --> Applicant : Display "Application Submitted"

... Time Passes ...

Owner -> React : View Project Requests List
React -> API : GET /api/projects/:id/requests
activate API
API -> DB : Query CollaborationRequests (projectId)
activate DB
DB --> API : Return requests list
deactivate DB
API --> React : 200 OK { success: true, data: { results } }
deactivate API

Owner -> React : Click "Accept Request"
React -> API : PATCH /api/requests/:id { status: "ACCEPTED" }
activate API

API -> API : Verify Owner identity & check teamSize capacity
API -> DB : Update Request status -> ACCEPTED
activate DB
DB --> API : Request updated
deactivate DB

API -> DB : Update Project memberIds ($addToSet: senderId)
activate DB
DB --> API : Member added to Project
deactivate DB

API --> React : 200 OK { success: true, data: updatedRequest }
deactivate API
React --> Owner : Display "Member Accepted & Added to Team"
@enduml
